<title>GERMANY: Pan-German Nov industry output jumps 1.6 pct m/m.</title>
<headline>Pan-German Nov industry output jumps 1.6 pct m/m.</headline>
<dateline>BONN 1997-01-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The economics ministry reported the following economic indicator:</p>
<p> PAN-GERMAN INDUSTRY OUTPUT  Nov 96     Oct 96	Nov 95</p>
<p> Month-on-month change(pct)   +1.6	 -0.7	 +1.2</p>
<p> Year-on-year		     +1.3	 +0.9	 -1.4</p>
<p> Index (base 1991)		99.5	 97.9	 98.2</p>
<p>NOTE - Figures are seasonally adjusted and provisional. The year-on-year figures are calculated by Reuters from Bundesbank statistics. @ The ministry gave the following details:</p>
<p>				    Nov 96		   Oct 96</p>
<p>				Index   Pct change  Index   Pct change</p>
<p> Mining			75.6	+0.8	75.0	+1.4</p>
<p> Manufacturing output    98.2	+2.3	96.0	-1.2</p>
<p> Incl:Intermed. goods   103.0	+2.4     100.6	-0.4</p>
<p>	Capital goods	96.9	+2.5	94.5	-2.3</p>
<p>	Consumer durables  86.7	+4.2	83.2	-1.8</p>
<p>	Consumer goods     95.2	+0.3	94.9	-0.8</p>
<p> Energy output	    104.9	unch     104.9	+2.3</p>
<p> Construction	     114.3	-2.0     116.6	+1.1 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 96 with Aug/Sept 96:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     unch</p>
<p> Manufacturing output		  -0.5</p>
<p> Construction			    +0.5</p>
<p> Capital goods			   -0.5</p>
<p> Mining				    +2.0</p>
<p> Energy output			   +0.5</p>
<p> Consumer durables and goods	 -2.0</p>
<p> Intermediate goods		    +0.5 @</p>
<p>Two month comparison Oct/Nov 1996 with Oct/Nov 1995:</p>
<p> Industrial output		     +1.0</p>
<p> Mining				    -3.9</p>
<p> Manufacturing output:		 +2.3</p>
<p>  Incl: Intermediate goods	   +3.0</p>
<p>	  Capital goods		  +2.5</p>
<p>	  Consumer durables	    +3.8</p>
<p>	  Consumer goods		 -0.4</p>
<p> Energy output			   +4.0</p>
<p> Construction			    -6.4</p>
<p>-- Bonn newsroom, 49-228-26097150</p>
</text>
